--- The `Damages` struct is Kenshi's core value-type data structure representing multi-channel physical trauma payloads. It is constructed during combat attacks, passed across animation hit callbacks, mitigated by armour calculations, and applied to character anatomical health systems.
---@class Damages
--- Scales the primary physical damage channels (`cut`, `blunt`, `pierce`, and `extraStun`) in-place by the specified multiplier. Does not scale `bleedMult` or `armourPenetration`. Used for critical strike multipliers, strength scaling, and body part toughness degradation.
---@field multiply fun(self: Damages, mult: number)
--- Calculates the absolute aggregate raw hitpoint damage represented by this payload by summing `cut`, `blunt`, and `pierce`. Used for floating combat text numbers, weapon tooltip comparisons, and threat aggregation calculations.
---@field total fun(self: Damages): number
--- Percentage factor (`0.0f` to `1.0f`) that bypasses the target's equipped armor defense layers during mitigation.
---@field armourPenetration number
--- Scalar multiplier applied to the target's bleeding rate calculation when laceration occurs. Default is `1.0f`.
---@field bleedMult number
--- Non-lethal concussive trauma. Contributes to temporary KO thresholds, unconsciousness time, and limb shock.
---@field blunt number
--- Lethal laceration and slicing damage. Direct contributor to open flesh wounds and immediate bleeding rates.
---@field cut number
--- Additional stun damage applied directly to character incapacitation meters without reducing structural hitpoints.
---@field extraStun number
--- High-velocity ballistic/harpoon penetration damage. Pierces armor plating with specialized damage mitigation curves.
---@field pierce number

