--- Master game state serialization, session persistence, and savegame management singleton in Kenshi. Manages save directories (`localSavePath`, `userSavePath`), active save slot metadata (`currentGame`), save/load/import modal dialog windows (`loadMenu`, `saveMenu`, `importMenu`), automated background save intervals (`autoSaveTimer`), version validation (`checkVersion`, `versionCode`), low-level world state serialization (`saveGame`, `loadGame`), and cross-version asset import filters (`importGame`, `importPlayerBuildings`).
---@class SaveManager
--- Queries whether any save, load, or import modal GUI window is currently open and visible on screen.
---@field isVisible fun(self: SaveManager): integer
--- Constructs (if necessary) and displays the modal Save Game GUI dialog window (`saveMenu`), populating current slot suggestions and screenshot previews.
---@field showSave fun(self: SaveManager)
--- Constructs and displays the modal Load Game GUI dialog window (`loadMenu`), scanning available saves and rendering save slot cards.
---@field showLoad fun(self: SaveManager)
--- Constructs and displays the modal Import Game GUI dialog window (`importMenu`), allowing player selection of import flags and source save files.
---@field showImport fun(self: SaveManager)
--- Closes and hides all active save, load, and import modal GUI windows, returning focus to the primary game viewport.
---@field hide fun(self: SaveManager)
--- Signals the engine to begin a new game session using scenario identifier `startId`. Sets pending signal `NEWGAME` and arms execution delay timer.
---@field newGame fun(self: SaveManager, startId: string)
--- Enqueues a game save operation targeting slot name `s`. If `autosave` is true, applies rotating autosave slot indexing. Sets pending signal `SAVEGAME`.
---@field save fun(self: SaveManager, s: string, autosave?: boolean)
--- Fast query checking whether any saved game directories exist in the local or user save directories.
---@field savesExist fun(self: SaveManager): boolean
--- Checks if a specific savegame slot `name` exists within filesystem path `location`.
---@field saveExists fun(self: SaveManager, location: string, name: string): boolean
--- Processes queued save, load, new game, or import operations and updates transition timers.
---@field execute fun(self: SaveManager)
--- Parses a semantic version string (e.g. "1.0.65") into a packed 32-bit integer version code suitable for numerical comparison.
---@field versionCode fun(self: SaveManager, version: string): integer
--- Per-frame tick updating the autosave timer. When the elapsed interval exceeds user configured settings (and autosave is unpaused), automatically triggers a rotating autosave.
---@field updateAutoSave fun(self: SaveManager)
--- Discovers and initializes filesystem directories for local game installation saves (`localSavePath`) and user AppData profile saves (`userSavePath`), establishing directory permissions and fallback paths.
---@field initialisePaths fun(self: SaveManager)
--- Low-level core save implementation. Serializes active world data, zone states, platoons, player buildings, research, faction relations, and camera transforms to `location/name`.
---@field saveGame fun(self: SaveManager, location: string, name: string): integer
--- Low-level core load implementation. Clears existing world state, resets zones and platoons, deserializes game objects, and instantiates character entities from `location/name`.
---@field loadGame fun(self: SaveManager, location: string, name: string): integer
--- Low-level core import implementation. Re-initializes a fresh base game world and merges player squads, buildings, research, relations, and NPC death states from source save `location/name` according to filter `flags`.
---@field importGame fun(self: SaveManager, location: string, name: string, flags: integer): integer
--- Imports player-owned buildings, outposts, and interior furniture placements from modern serialized building records (`path/file`).
---@field importPlayerBuildings fun(self: SaveManager, path: string, file: string): integer
--- Legacy import routine migrating player-constructed buildings and outposts from older Kenshi save formats into current structure definitions.
---@field importOldPlayerBuildings fun(self: SaveManager, path: string, name: string): integer
--- Retrieves the global singleton instance of `SaveManager`. Lazily allocates the instance on first invocation via Ogre general allocator if uninitialized.
---@field getSingleton fun(): SaveManager|nil
--- Enqueues a game load operation from descriptor `s`, with an option to reset all squad member positions to camera focus point. Sets pending signal `LOADGAME`.
---@field load fun(self: SaveManager, name: SaveInfo|string, arg2?: boolean)
--- Enqueues a game import operation from save slot `s` using configuration bitmask `_flags` (`IMPORT_BUILDINGS`, `IMPORT_RESEARCH`, `IMPORT_NPC_STATES`, etc.). Sets pending signal `IMPORTGAME`.
---@field import fun(self: SaveManager, s: SaveInfo, _flags: integer)
--- Reads and parses save header files (`info.dat` / `quick.save`) into `SaveInfo& info`, extracting game time, squad size, money, and mod dependencies.
---@field loadInfo fun(self: SaveManager, info: SaveInfo): boolean
--- Validates version compatibility of savegame `info` against current engine version, detecting whether migration or warnings are required.
---@field checkVersion fun(self: SaveManager, info: SaveInfo): boolean
--- Returns the name or folder identifier of the currently loaded active game session (`currentGame`).
---@field getCurrentGame fun(self: SaveManager): string
--- Returns the active filesystem directory path currently configured for saving and loading games.
---@field getSavePath fun(self: SaveManager): string
--- Scans the default active save directory, populating `list` with `SaveInfo` descriptors for all discovered save slots.
---@field scanGames fun(self: SaveManager, location: Lektor<SaveInfo>|SaveManager|string, list?: Lektor<SaveInfo>|SaveManager|boolean, loadDetails?: boolean): integer
--- Elapsed time counter tracking autosave trigger intervals.
---@field autoSaveTimer number
--- Directory or slot identifier of currently active game session.
---@field currentGame string
--- Frame delay countdown before scheduled save/load operation executes.
---@field delay integer
--- Bitmask configuration flags (`RESET_POSITION`, `IMPORT_SQUAD`, `IMPORT_BUILDINGS`, etc.).
---@field flags integer
--- Modal GUI dialog for configuring import options and starting game imports.
---@field importMenu lightuserdata
--- Modal GUI dialog for browsing and loading saved games.
---@field loadMenu lightuserdata
--- Base directory path for local saves within application install.
---@field localSavePath string
--- Directory path containing target savegame slot.
---@field location string
--- Target save slot filename or new game scenario name.
---@field name string
--- Flag suppressing autosave timer countdown during menus or dialogue.
---@field pauseAutoSaveTimer boolean
--- Modal GUI dialog for naming and saving current game state.
---@field saveMenu lightuserdata
--- Version string token recorded in save file headers.
---@field saveVersion string
--- Pending operation signal code (`SAVEGAME=1`, `LOADGAME=2`, `IMPORTGAME=3`, `NEWGAME=4`).
---@field signal integer
--- User profile appdata savegame directory path.
---@field userSavePath string
--- Nested enum table `SaveManager.Flags`.
---@field Flags SaveManager.Flags
--- Nested enum table `SaveManager.Signal`.
---@field Signal SaveManager.Signal

